      "math_academy_id": "q-126016",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =P(3\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}]}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
